<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    OstrichChallenge - Loading Screen Tips

    Ported from the Hospital Challenge's Localization.csv "# LOADING SCREEN TIPS" section, which
    is where this pattern already works. Fril, 8 Oct 2026: "Id also like to add the rotating
    Loading Screen tips ... and the (# UI & MENU - SPAWN / RESPAWN SCREEN) that we have in the
    Hospital localisation.csv. Obviously tailored to this challenge."

    HOW THE GAME READS THIS, verified against the vanilla 3.3 loadingscreen.xml and
    Localization.csv rather than assumed:

      - vanilla loadingscreen.xml holds <backgrounds> and <tips>, and each tip is a bare
        <tip key="..." /> under /doc/tips. Nothing else. There is no weighting and no ordering.
      - the key names the BODY string, and the same key plus "_title" names the heading. Vanilla
        carries 41 tip keys and 41 matching _title keys, which is how the pairing was confirmed.
        Only 40 of them are in the rotation: loadingTipJournalEntries is commented out in
        vanilla's own loadingscreen.xml, so "41 tips" would have been wrong.
      - so tips need no DLL at all. FrilOstrichRotateLoadingscreens rotates the BACKGROUND IMAGES
        and has nothing to do with this file.

    v1.92.2: THIS REPLACES THE LIST, IT NO LONGER APPENDS TO IT.

    v1.92.0 appended, leaving vanilla's 40 active tips in the rotation alongside these 15. Fril, 8 Oct
    2026: "Im seeing vanilla loading screen tips as well as ours". The remove below strips every
    tip vanilla ships before ours go in, so the rotation is the hotel's own and nothing else.

    That is also the right answer on the merits, not just the requested one. Several vanilla tips
    are flatly untrue here, because the ESC guide says "There is nobody to trade with in here and
    nothing to build your way out with": loadingTipQuestSharing, loadingTipTwitchIntegration, loadingTipSeeds,
    loadingTipApiary, loadingTipDewCollector and loadingTipCollectors among them.

    TWO THINGS THIS RELIES ON, BOTH READ OUT OF THE 3.3 IL RATHER THAN ASSUMED:

      - XmlPatchMethods.RemoveByXPath calls GetXpathResults, foreaches the result set, and per
        match calls XNode.AddAfterSelf (an XComment marking the removal) then XNode.Remove.
        So ONE remove with a multi-match xpath removes EVERY match. "/doc/tips/tip" takes all 40.
      - XmlPatcher.PatchXml foreaches XContainer.Elements() and calls singlePatch per element,
        and Elements() yields in document order. So patches inside one file apply top to bottom.

    THE ORDER OF THE TWO PATCHES BELOW THEREFORE MATTERS: the remove must come first. Reversed,
    it would strip our own tips along with vanilla's and leave an empty rotation.

    TO PUT ANY VANILLA TIP BACK, delete the remove and list the ones you want kept individually,
    or add the single key back in the append block. Nothing is lost: vanilla's own
    loadingscreen.xml is untouched on disk and this file only patches it at load.
-->
<configs>

    <!-- Every tip vanilla ships. Matches all <tip> children of /doc/tips, not one key. -->
    <remove xpath="/doc/tips/tip" />

    <append xpath="/doc/tips">

        <!-- The job -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip01" />   <!-- The Register            -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip02" />   <!-- The Bell                -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip03" />   <!-- Work Downwards          -->

        <!-- Him -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip04" />   <!-- He Hunts By Sound       -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip05" />   <!-- Quiet Is Not Safe       -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip06" />   <!-- He Learns the Building  -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip07" />   <!-- He Gets Back Up         -->

        <!-- The way out -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip08" />   <!-- He Has the Key          -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip09" />   <!-- Zero, Then the Window   -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip14" />   <!-- The City Is Not a Way Out -->

        <!-- Living in the building -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip10" />   <!-- Nothing Is Coming       -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip11" />   <!-- The Radio               -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip12" />   <!-- Rooms Refill            -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip13" />   <!-- Fifteen Floors          -->
        <tip key="ostrichLoadingTip15" />   <!-- Your Kit                -->

    </append>

</configs>
